gy","def-projective-object","def-projective-resolution-in-an-abelian-category","def-regular-and-critical-points-and-values","def-smooth-bundle-metric","def-subspace-topology-top","fs-enough-projectives-selects-a-projective-resolution-functor-on-all-objects","prop-a-projective-object-has-a-length-zero-projective-resolution","prop-an-additive-functor-applies-degreewise-to-complexes-and-chain-maps","prop-an-additive-functor-preserves-zero-morphisms","prop-comparison-maps-respect-composition-up-to-homotopy","prop-comparison-of-the-identity-is-homotopic-to-the-identity","prop-homology-respects-identities-and-composition","prop-the-iterated-free-module-resolution-is-canonical-in-zf","thm-a-chain-map-induces-a-well-defined-map-on-homology","thm-an-additive-functor-preserves-finite-biproducts","thm-an-exact-functor-commutes-with-homology","thm-chain-homotopic-maps-induce-the-same-map-on-homology","thm-coordinate-formula-for-the-differential-of-a-function","thm-euclidean-implicit-function-theorem","thm-euclidean-inverse-function-theorem","thm-euler-poincare-formula-for-finite-free-complexes","thm-heine-borel-rn","thm-hom-is-left-exact-in-each-variable","thm-homology-is-an-additive-functor","thm-horseshoe-lemma-for-injective-resolutions","thm-horseshoe-lemma-for-projective-resolutions","thm-injective-comparison-map-exists","thm-injective-comparison-maps-are-unique-up-to-cochain-homotopy","thm-injective-resolutions-of-the-same-object-are-homotopy-equivalent-under-that-object","thm-long-exact-sequence-in-cohomology","thm-long-exact-sequence-in-homology","thm-metric-hausdorff-separation","thm-projective-comparison-map-exists","thm-projective-comparison-maps-are-unique-up-to-chain-homotopy","thm-projective-resolutions-of-the-same-object-are-homotopy-equivalent-over-that-object","thm-sylvesters-law-of-inertia","thm-the-category-of-complexes-in-an-additive-category-is-additive","thm-the-opposite-of-an-abelian-category-is-abelian"],"conventions":[{"convention":"A supplied projective or injective resolution datum is extra objectwise structure on a specified class, not a canonical global selection of resolutions.","fixed_by":"def-supplied-projective-resolution-datum","matters_for":["def-left-derived-object-relative-to-projective-resolution-data","def-left-derived-map-relative-to-resolution-data","thm-left-derived-functors-from-two-supplied-resolution-data-are-naturally-isomorphic","fs-enough-projectives-implies-a-canonical-resolution-for-every-object"]},{"convention":"Left derived objects use homology of the deleted projective resolution, while right derived objects use cohomology of the deleted injective resolution; both are defined in all integer degrees.","fixed_by":"def-left-derived-object-relative-to-projective-resolution-data","matters_for":["prop-negative-derived-degrees-vanish-for-one-sided-resolutions","thm-zero-th-left-derived-functor-of-a-right-exact-functor-recovers-the-functor","thm-zero-th-right-derived-functor-of-a-left-exact-functor-recovers-the-functor","prop-contravariant-derived-functors-are-derived-on-the-opposite-category"]},{"convention":"An abstract simplicial complex contains the empty face and every singleton vertex face; this page does not replace that language by delta-complexes.","fixed_by":"def-abstract-simplicial-complex","matters_for":["def-geometric-realization-of-an-abstract-simplicial-complex","def-simplicial-chain-groups-and-boundary","ex-a-delta-complex-structure-on-the-torus"]},{"convention":"The realization consists of finitely supported barycentric-coordinate functions whose support is a simplex and carries the weak topology determined simplexwise.","fixed_by":"def-geometric-realization-of-an-abstract-simplicial-complex","matters_for":["prop-a-finite-simplicial-complex-has-compact-hausdorff-realization","lem-the-realization-of-a-simplicial-map-is-continuous-and-functorial","lem-contiguous-simplicial-maps-have-homotopic-realizations","prop-zero-th-simplicial-homology-is-free-on-connected-components"]},{"convention":"The unaugmented simplicial chain groups are zero in degrees below zero, and the stated boundary convention is the alternating omission order.","fixed_by":"def-simplicial-chain-groups-and-boundary","matters_for":["thm-the-simplicial-boundary-squares-to-zero","def-simplicial-cycles-boundaries-and-homology","def-augmentation-and-reduced-simplicial-homology","def-induced-simplicial-chain-map"]},{"convention":"Reduced simplicial homology is the homology of the augmentation C_0(K) to Z; a vertexless complex has reduced homology Z in degree -1 and zero elsewhere.","fixed_by":"def-augmentation-and-reduced-simplicial-homology","matters_for":["lem-the-simplicial-augmentation-is-a-chain-map","lem-the-augmented-simplicial-chain-complex-of-a-simplex-is-contractible","cor-the-simplex-has-zero-reduced-simplicial-homology","ex-simplicial-homology-of-a-point-and-an-edge"]},{"convention":"The intrinsic Hessian is defined only at a critical point by second coordinate derivatives, and its chart independence is by congruence.","fixed_by":"def-hessian-of-a-function-at-a-critical-point","matters_for":["lem-coordinate-change-congruence-for-the-critical-hessian","lem-critical-hessian-agrees-with-the-levi-civita-hessian","def-nondegenerate-critical-point-nullity-index-and-coindex"]},{"convention":"Morse index is the maximal dimension of a negative-definite Hessian subspace, coindex is the positive-definite analogue, and nullity is the kernel dimension.","fixed_by":"def-nondegenerate-critical-point-nullity-index-and-coindex","matters_for":["lem-sylvester-inertia-makes-morse-index-intrinsic","thm-morse-lemma","cor-local-extrema-and-saddles-from-the-morse-index","cor-index-and-coindex-swap-under-negation","ex-height-on-a-torus-with-four-critical-points"]},{"convention":"On a zero-dimensional manifold every point is a nondegenerate critical point of index and coindex zero; the empty zero-manifold has no critical points.","fixed_by":"rem-zero-dimensional-morse-convention","matters_for":["thm-morse-lemma","cor-local-extrema-and-saddles-from-the-morse-index","ex-standard-quadratic-form-of-each-morse-index","ex-the-empty-and-zero-dimensional-morse-cases"]}],"load_bearing":[{"id":"thm-morse-lemma","statement":"Let f:M to R be smooth, let p be a nondegenerate critical point of index lambda on an n-manifold. There are local coordinates centered at p in which f=f(p)-sum_{i=1}^lambda (x^i)^2+sum_{i=lambda+1}^n (x^i)^2.","used_by":["cor-local-extrema-and-saddles-from-the-morse-index","cor-local-level-set-cone-at-a-morse-critical-point","ex-standard-quadratic-form-of-each-morse-index"]},{"id":"def-simplicial-chain-groups-and-boundary","statement":"C_n(K) is the free abelian group on oriented n-simplices, with the orientation-sign relation, and the boundary is the alternating vertex-omission formula.","used_by":["thm-the-simplicial-boundary-squares-to-zero","def-simplicial-cycles-boundaries-and-homology","def-augmentation-and-reduced-simplicial-homology","def-induced-simplicial-chain-map","ex-simplicial-homology-of-a-point-and-an-edge"]},{"id":"thm-left-derived-functors-relative-to-supplied-data-are-additive-functors","statement":"For every n in Z, A maps to L_n^P F(A) and u maps to L_n^P F(u) define an additive functor on the domain of P.","used_by":["prop-a-natural-transformation-induces-natural-transformations-of-left-derived-functors","thm-left-derived-functors-from-two-supplied-resolution-data-are-naturally-isomorphic","thm-zero-th-left-derived-functor-of-a-right-exact-functor-recovers-the-functor","prop-derived-functors-commute-with-finite-biproducts"]},{"id":"thm-right-derived-functors-relative-to-supplied-data-are-additive-functors","statement":"For every n in Z, A maps to R_I^n F(A) and u maps to R_I^n F(u) define an additive functor on the domain of I.","used_by":["prop-a-natural-transformation-induces-natural-transformations-of-right-derived-functors","thm-right-derived-functors-from-two-supplied-injective-resolution-data-are-naturally-isomorphic","thm-zero-th-right-derived-functor-of-a-left-exact-functor-recovers-the-functor","prop-derived-functors-commute-with-finite-biproducts"]},{"id":"thm-acyclic-resolution-theorem-for-right-derived-functors","statement":"Under its supplied-data and cycle-domain hypotheses, R_I^n F(A) is canonically isomorphic to H^n(F(J^bullet_del)) for every n>=0.","used_by":["cor-adapted-classes-compute-derived-functors"]},{"id":"def-abstract-simplicial-complex","statement":"An abstract simplicial complex is a vertex set V with a downward-closed family K of finite subsets containing the empty face and every singleton vertex.","used_by":["def-geometric-realization-of-an-abstract-simplicial-complex","def-simplicial-map-and-its-geometric-realization","def-orientation-of-a-simplex","def-simplicial-subcomplex-star-closure-and-link"]},{"id":"thm-the-simplicial-boundary-squares-to-zero","statement":"For every simplicial complex K and every n, partial_(n-1) partial_n=0:C_n(K) to C_(n-2)(K).","used_by":["def-simplicial-cycles-boundaries-and-homology","lem-the-simplicial-augmentation-is-a-chain-map"]},{"id":"prop-zero-th-simplicial-homology-is-free-on-connected-components","statement":"For every simplicial complex K, H_0^simp(K) is the free abelian group on the connected components of |K|.","used_by":["ex-simplicial-homology-of-the-tetrahedron-boundary"]},{"id":"def-nondegenerate-critical-point-nullity-index-and-coindex","statement":"Nullity is the Hessian-kernel dimension; nondegeneracy means nullity zero; index and coindex are the maximal dimensions of negative- and positive-definite Hessian subspaces.","used_by":["lem-sylvester-inertia-makes-morse-index-intrinsic","def-morse-function-and-excellent-morse-function","thm-morse-lemma","ex-height-on-the-sphere-is-a-perfect-morse-function","ex-height-on-a-torus-with-four-critical-points"]}],"published_dependencies":[{"id":"cor-a-contractible-complex-is-acyclic","used_for":"Acyclicity after constructing augmented simplicial contractions.","opened":